# Rate limits for a Bowrain server under the end-to-end suites. Both stacks
# that run them read this one file: CI's (bowrain/e2e/server/compose.yaml) and
# the local one (make -C bowrain stack-up-e2e, through compose.e2e.yaml).
#
# The suites call the pre-auth and auth endpoints far faster than a person
# does: a device-auth flow per spec file, an anonymous project per claim test,
# a sign-in per Go test. The production caps (bowrain/server/
# middleware_ratelimit.go) answer them with 429. The caps themselves are
# covered by Go tests, so these give the suites headroom. Never use them on a
# real deployment.
BOWRAIN_RL_ANON_PER_MIN=600
BOWRAIN_RL_ANON_BURST=100
BOWRAIN_RL_AUTH_PER_MIN=600
BOWRAIN_RL_AUTH_BURST=100
